{
  "_comment": "Genesis seed pack (Spanish) for the action map (V2-539). Every entry is an UNAMBIGUOUS, whole-utterance command mapped to one allowlisted direct action. Phrases are normalized on import (accents/punctuation don't matter here). Courtesy/word-order variants are separate entries ON PURPOSE — the matcher is not allowed to understand. When a phrase could plausibly mean something richer than the mapped action, it does NOT belong in this pack: the model handles it.",
  "version": 4,
  "grids": [
    {
      "_comment": "VERB x OBJECT grid for mensajeria's LENSES (V2-545). «Abreme el Telegram» is not «show the card»: WhatsApp/Telegram/correo are VIEWS OF a card, and the model reads them as card names because they are also the widget's aliases - measured live, three turns of «Aqui lo tienes» over an unmoved card. Expanded into ordinary exact-match entries at import; a view op also brings the card up (executor), so one order gets both halves. `$` is filled with the value.",
      "verbs": [
        "abre",
        "ábreme",
        "ábreme ahora",
        "muestra",
        "muéstrame",
        "muéstrame ahora",
        "enséñame",
        "enséñame ahora",
        "ponme"
      ],
